@PrasannaJatla1 The end-of-life of a pod which has long-running connections might not force-close those connections. 

You have a couple options.  You could set up some sort of max-lifetime at the ALB, so it doesn't keep backend-connections open indefinitely.  You could have the pod backend close the connection at some point (e.g. once you receive SIGTERM, you can still accept connections and serve them, but then close the connection).

There's not much that kube-proxy can realistically do here.

